First details emerge from Square Enix’s private Guardians of the Galaxy presentation:

- The game appears to run on the same engine as Marvel's Avengers;  
- A single-player narrative experience with no microtransactions or DLC;  
- You play exclusively as Peter Quill—no co-op and no switching between characters;  
- Combat feels familiar to Marvel's Avengers, but Quill relies mostly on shooting and his rocket boots;  
- Nonlinear structure, though the story leads to a single, fixed ending;  
- The Guardians have been together for several years when the game begins. The galaxy has recently endured a massive war. As the story starts, the crew is scrambling to make money—only to accidentally trigger a chain of events that could destroy everything.

